{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "CircleCI JUnit results not stored or exported",
    "Explanation": [
      "The 'Run tests' step log shows 'Wrote ~/project/results/test_results.xml' before the step exits, so the results file was produced (results_produced = true). The step then runs `exit 1`: steps.txt lists 'Run tests FAILED' and the log ends with 'CircleCI received exit code 1', so the job did not succeed (job_green = false). The config's steps are only `checkout` and one `run` step. There is no `store_test_results` step, so nothing feeds the Test Summary tab (missing_store_test_results = true). There is also no `store_artifacts` step, so the file is never exported as an artifact (missing_store_artifacts = true). The requirement covers both reporting surfaces, so the fix is to add both steps pointing at ~/project/results (for example `store_test_results: path: ~/project/results` and `store_artifacts: path: ~/project/results`). Because 'Run tests' fails, both steps also need `when: always` so they still run after the failure. Removing `exit 1` alone would only affect the job status and would not report the results; there is no `upload` setting involved."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"fix\": \"add_store_test_results_and_store_artifacts\",",
      "  \"job_green\": false,",
      "  \"missing_store_artifacts\": true,",
      "  \"missing_store_test_results\": true,",
      "  \"results_produced\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"fix\": \"add_store_test_results_and_store_artifacts\",",
        "  \"job_green\": false,",
        "  \"missing_store_artifacts\": true,",
        "  \"missing_store_test_results\": true,",
        "  \"results_produced\": true",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
