{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy ran on non-production branch",
    "Explanation": [
      "The run shows the workflow build-test-and-deploy finished SUCCESS with all three jobs green, so pipeline_green is true. However, the run was on branch 'koans-08-branch-filters', not 'production', yet the deploy job ran (and executed 'echo \"Deploy complete\"'). The requirement says deploy must run only for commits to production, so the behaviour is incorrect. The config's deploy workflow entry has only 'requires: [test-production]' and no branch filter; requires does not restrict branches. The fix is to add 'filters: branches: only: production' to the deploy entry in the workflow. Branch filters belong on the workflow job entry, not the job definition. An 'ignore' list of non-production branches would be fragile and would not reliably limit deploy to production. build and test-production need no restriction, and leaving them unfiltered keeps the production workflow green because deploy's required job test-production still runs there."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
        "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
        "}"
      ]
