{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy ran on untagged branch push",
    "Explanation": [
      "This run did not behave as required. The workflow ran from a push to the branch `koans-09-tag-filters` via an API trigger, with no tag shown. build, test and deploy all show SUCCESS, so the pipeline was green. But deploy ran on an untagged branch push, which the requirement forbids. The config has no `filters` on any job, so deploy runs on every branch push. CircleCI also does not run jobs for tag pushes unless each job has a matching `filters.tags` entry. So pushing `beta-main-0.1.1` would not currently deploy. Deploy needs a tag filter that accepts only beta tags (e.g. `only: /^beta-.*/`) and `branches: ignore: /.*/`. Because deploy requires test, which requires build, build and test also need a tag filter matching beta tags. Otherwise they would not run on the tag push and deploy would never be reached. Build and test can keep running on branches, since branches run by default. So the change applies to all jobs: add a beta-only tag filter everywhere, plus the branch ignore on deploy."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
        "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
        "}"
      ]
