{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Apps not persisted to workspace for deploy",
    "Explanation": [
      "Per workflow.txt, build-linux, build-mac and build-windows all show SUCCESS, while deploy shows FAILED, and the workflow is FAILED. In deploy's 'Verify apps present' step (job.log), the find output after attaching the workspace lists only ./meta/linux/build.txt, ./meta/mac/build.txt and ./meta/windows/build.txt. No app/* files are present, so `test -f app/linux/app.linux` returned exit code 1. The cause is in config.yml: each build job's persist_to_workspace lists only its meta/\u003cplatform\u003e directory. The app/\u003cplatform\u003e directory that holds the generated app file is never persisted, so the attached workspace cannot contain the apps. The fix is to add app/linux, app/windows and app/mac to the persist_to_workspace paths of the matching build jobs. The alternatives do not meet the requirement. Storing artifacts only on the build jobs means deploy still has no apps, and the requirement is that deploy verifies and uploads them. Fixing only one platform leaves two tests failing. Changing only attach_workspace does nothing, because the files were never persisted. Removing the verify step would make the job pass without the apps actually being available, which does not satisfy the requirement."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"builds_green\": true,",
      "  \"deploy_green\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"persist_app_paths\",",
      "  \"workspace_had_apps\": false",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"builds_green\": true,",
        "  \"deploy_green\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"persist_app_paths\",",
        "  \"workspace_had_apps\": false",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
